# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 286-287 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, RUN 3, 2026-09-26): THE LASHES — no peace out of strife (Abram's
# and Lot's herdsmen), the parties, against their will, the class of the flogged by the muzzle's prototype, lying down, a third and two parts, the eyes on him,
# one sanction (no death, no payment with the lashes), forty by a count that borders it, not the ground nor the garment, one at a time, the court's estimate,
# the first blow, the befouled exempt, THE BROTHER RESTORED and the excision lifted, the three homilies of Makkot 3:15-16 (286 — seventeen rows, the largest
# piska of the four chapters); THE MUZZLE — every beast, not the man, every labor with the four conditions, hands feet and body (287). Every row READ WHOLE in
# both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_. Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(286, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN THERE IS A QUARREL BETWEEN MEN" (25:1) — NO PEACE COMES OUT OF STRIFE; GENESIS 13:7 "THERE WAS A QUARREL BETWEEN THE HERDSMEN OF ABRAM\'S CATTLE AND OF LOT\'S" — WHAT MADE LOT PART FROM THE RIGHTEOUS ONE? STRIFE; WHAT MADE THIS ONE BE FLOGGED? STRIFE. The head row of piska 286 — the edge clean (285:4 stopped at 24:21) — READ BEFORE at Genesis 29\'s ledger (the separation of Abram and Lot), REREAD WHOLE here ({SP_(286, 1, "אין", "שלום", "יוצא", "מתוך", "מריבה")} "no peace comes out of strife"; {SP_(286, 1, "מי", "גרם", "ללוט", "לפרש", "מן", "הצדיק")} "what caused Lot to part from the righteous one?"; {SP_(286, 1, "מי", "גרם", "לזה", "ללקות")} "what caused this one to be flogged?"): the tape\'s own Genesis 13 read back as the cause of every court case — the quarrel the trigger of the lashes\' cell (the design\'s DV25-01). Reread.')
srow(286, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"BETWEEN MEN" — ONLY MEN? A MAN WITH A WOMAN, A WOMAN WITH A MAN, TWO WOMEN — WHENCE? "THEY COME TO JUDGMENT" — ANYONE. ({SP_(286, 2, "איש", "עם", "אשה", "ואשה", "עם", "איש")} "a man with a woman and a woman with a man"; {SP_(286, 2, "ושתי", "נשים", "זו", "עם", "זו")} "and two women with each other"): the parties\' class every person — 249:1\'s sex parameter reversed. Fresh.')
srow(286, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY JUDGE THEM" — AGAINST THEIR WILL. ({SP_(286, 3, "בעל", "כרחם")} "against their will"): the court\'s jurisdiction not consensual. Fresh.')
srow(286, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND JUSTIFY THE RIGHTEOUS" — ARE ALL THE GUILTY FLOGGED? "IF THE WICKED DESERVES FLOGGING" (25:2) — SOMETIMES YES, SOMETIMES NO; WHICH? "MUZZLE NOT AN OX" (25:4): AS THE MUZZLE IS A NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT AND FLOGGED, SO EVERY NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT; OR EVERY ONE WITH A "RISE AND DO"? AS THE MUZZLE HAS NO "RISE AND DO" AND IS FLOGGED, SO EVERY NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT WITHOUT A REMEDY. R. SHIMON: JUSTIFY HIM SO HE NOT BE FLOGGED? "IF HE DESERVES FLOGGING" — SOMETIMES. ({SP_(286, 4, "יכול", "כל", "המרשעים", "לוקים")} "might all the guilty be flogged?"; {SP_(286, 4, "פעמים", "לוקה", "פעמים", "אינו", "לוקה")} "sometimes flogged, sometimes not"; {SP_(286, 4, "מה", "חסימת", "שור", "מיחדת")} "as the muzzling of the ox is distinctive"; {SP_(286, 4, "שאין", "בה", "קום", "עשה")} "which has no \'rise and do\'"; {SP_(286, 4, "צדקהו", "כדי", "שלא", "יהא", "לוקה")} "justify him so that he not be flogged"): THE CLASS OF THE FLOGGABLE fixed by the muzzle\'s prototype — a prohibition with no positive remedy (Makkot 3\'s principle, the Tosefta the English cites); 25:4\'s verse read into 25:1-3 by adjacency — the muzzle the lashes\' key. Fresh.')
srow(286, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE JUDGE LAYS HIM DOWN" (25:2) — THEY DO NOT FLOG ONE STANDING. ({SP_(286, 5, "אין", "מלקים", "מעומד")} "they do not flog one standing"): the posture; 25:2 carries no head — its rows inside 286. Fresh.')
srow(286, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND FLOGS HIM" — A THIRD BEFORE HIM AND TWO PARTS BEHIND. ({SP_(286, 6, "שליש", "לפניו", "ושתי", "ידות", "מאחריו")} "a third before him and two parts behind him"): Makkot 3:13\'s row (the English\'s "//") — the blows\' division a parameter. Fresh.')
srow(286, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"BEFORE HIM" — FLOGGED WITH THE JUDGE\'S EYES ON HIM, NOT ELSEWHERE; FLOGGED AND KILLED? "AS HIS WICKEDNESS DESERVES" — NOT FLOGGED AND KILLED; FLOGGED AND PAYING? — NOT FLOGGED AND PAYING. ({SP_(286, 7, "ועיניו", "בו")} "with his eyes on him"; {SP_(286, 7, "אין", "לוקה", "ומת")} "not flogged and killed"; {SP_(286, 7, "אין", "לוקה", "ומשלם")} "not flogged and paying"): THE ONE-SANCTION RULE — lashes exclude death and exclude payment (Makkot 1:2 and Ketubot 3:1\'s principle, the answer sheet\'s) — the compile\'s parameter on every fine beside a flogging (22:19\'s hundred, 22:29\'s fifty). Fresh.')
srow(286, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"FORTY" (25:3) — A FULL FORTY? "BY NUMBER, FORTY" — A COUNT THAT BORDERS ON FORTY; R. JUDAH: A FULL FORTY — WHERE THE EXTRA ONE? BETWEEN HIS SHOULDERS. ({SP_(286, 8, "יכול", "ארבעים", "שלמות")} "might it be a full forty?"; {SP_(286, 8, "מנין", "שהוא", "סוכם", "את", "הארבעים")} "a count that borders on the forty"; {SP_(286, 8, "היכן", "הוא", "לוקה", "את", "היתרה")} "where does he take the extra one?"; {SP_(286, 8, "בין", "כתפיו")} "between his shoulders"): THE PARSER\'S [40] READ AS THIRTY-NINE by the two verses\' seam ("by number" closing 25:2, "forty" opening 25:3 — the English\'s note on the order) — Makkot 3:10 the answer sheet\'s parameter (the design\'s DV25-01), R. Judah\'s forty the dissent. Fresh.')
srow(286, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL STRIKE HIM" — NOT THE GROUND; NOT HIS GARMENT; NOT TWO AS ONE. ({SP_(286, 9, "ולא", "על", "הקרקע")} "and not on the ground"; {SP_(286, 9, "ולא", "על", "כסותו")} "and not on his garment"; {SP_(286, 9, "אין", "מלקים", "שנים", "כאחד")} "they do not flog two as one"): the pronoun\'s three exclusions — the body, bare, one at a time. Fresh.')
srow(286, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL NOT ADD" — IF HE ADDED HE TRANSGRESSES A PROHIBITION; ONLY OVER THE COUNT? OVER ANY ESTIMATE THE COURT ESTIMATED — "LEST HE ADD". ({SP_(286, 10, "אם", "הוסיף", "עובר", "בלא", "תעשה")} "if he added he transgresses a prohibition"; {SP_(286, 10, "על", "כל", "אמד", "ואמד", "שאמדוהו", "בית", "דין")} "over any estimate the court estimated for him"): THE ESTIMATE (omed) — the count set below forty by the court\'s judgment of his strength (Makkot 3:11) — a PARAMETER per case; the officer\'s excess an offense. Fresh.')
srow(286, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"A GREAT BLOW" — ONLY A GREAT ONE? A LIGHT ONE WHENCE? "OVER THESE"; WHY "GREAT"? THE FIRST IS NOT A GREAT BLOW. ({SP_(286, 11, "מכה", "מועטת", "מנין")} "a light blow — whence?"; {SP_(286, 11, "שאין", "הראשונה", "מכה", "רבה")} "the first is not a great blow"): the blows equal, none heavier. Fresh.')
srow(286, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOUR BROTHER IS DEGRADED BEFORE YOUR EYES" — HENCE: IF HE BEFOULED HIMSELF WITH EXCREMENT OR URINE HE IS EXEMPT; R. JUDAH: THE MAN WITH EXCREMENT, THE WOMAN WITH URINE. ({SP_(286, 12, "נתקלקל", "בין", "ברעי", "בין", "במים", "פטור")} "if he befouled himself with excrement or with urine, he is exempt"; {SP_(286, 12, "האיש", "ברעי", "והאשה", "במים")} "the man with excrement, the woman with urine"): Makkot 3:14 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — the degradation the sentence\'s end, the rest remitted; 25:3 carries no head. Fresh.')
srow(286, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "YOUR BROTHER IS DEGRADED" — ONCE FLOGGED HE IS YOUR BROTHER; HENCE: ALL LIABLE TO EXCISION WHO WERE FLOGGED ARE FREED OF THEIR EXCISION. ({SP_(286, 13, "משלקה", "הרי", "הוא", "אחיך")} "once flogged he is your brother"; {SP_(286, 13, "כל", "חיבי", "כרתות", "שלקו", "נפטרו", "מידי", "כרתם")} "all liable to excision who were flogged are freed of their excision"): Makkot 3:15 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — THE STATUS EFFECT of the lashes: the wicked becomes the brother, the heavenly sanction lifted — the compile\'s effect on the person (the design\'s (f)). Fresh.')
srow(286, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'R. HANANIAH B. GAMLIEL: ALL THE DAY SCRIPTURE CALLS HIM WICKED — "IF THE WICKED DESERVES FLOGGING"; ONCE FLOGGED IT CALLS HIM YOUR BROTHER — "YOUR BROTHER IS DEGRADED". ({SP_(286, 14, "כל", "היום", "הכתוב", "קורא", "אותו", "רשע")} "all the day Scripture calls him wicked"; {SP_(286, 14, "אבל", "משלקה", "הכתוב", "קורא", "אותו", "אחיך")} "but once flogged Scripture calls him your brother"): the two names of one man in two verses — the status change read from the nouns (Makkot 3:15). Fresh.')
srow(286, 15, 'CONTEXT', f'R. SHIMON: FROM ITS OWN PLACE IT IS DECIDED — LEVITICUS 18:29 "CUT OFF" AND 18:5 "LIVE BY THEM"; AN A FORTIORI: IF THE LESSER MEASURE OF PUNISHMENT JOINS ONE TO THE TRANSGRESSORS\' JUDGMENT, ONE WHO JOINS THE DOERS OF A COMMANDMENT ALL THE MORE. ({SP_(286, 15, "ממקומו", "הוא", "מכרע")} "from its own place it is decided"; {SP_(286, 15, "קל", "וחמר")} "an a fortiori argument"; {SP_(286, 15, "הנטפל", "לעושי", "מצוה")} "he who joins the doers of a commandment"): the homily on the lifted excision — Makkot 3:15\'s continuation. Fresh.')
srow(286, 16, 'CONTEXT', f'R. SHIMON B. RABBI: "ONLY BE STRONG NOT TO EAT THE BLOOD" (12:23) — IF ONE WHO KEEPS FROM BLOOD, WHICH A MAN\'S SOUL RECOILS FROM, IS REWARDED, ONE WHO KEEPS FROM ROBBERY AND FORBIDDEN UNIONS, WHICH THE SOUL CRAVES, ALL THE MORE — FOR HIM AND HIS GENERATIONS TO THE END. READ BEFORE at chapter 12\'s ledger (the blood), REREAD WHOLE here ({SP_(286, 16, "מה", "הדם", "שנפשו", "של", "אדם", "חתה", "ממנו")} "as the blood, from which a man\'s soul recoils"; {SP_(286, 16, "גזל", "ועריות")} "robbery and forbidden unions"; {SP_(286, 16, "עד", "סוף", "כל", "הדורות")} "to the end of all the generations"): Makkot 3:15\'s a fortiori on abstention — the blood\'s verse the measure. Reread.')
srow(286, 17, 'CONTEXT', f'RABBI: PSALM 15:1-5 "WHO SHALL DWELL IN YOUR TENT … HIS SILVER HE GAVE NOT AT INTEREST" AND EZEKIEL 18:5-9 "A MAN WHO IS RIGHTEOUS … HE SHALL SURELY LIVE" — WHAT DID THIS ONE DO? WHOEVER SITS AND DOES NOT TRANSGRESS IS REWARDED AS ONE WHO DOES A COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(286, 17, "וכי", "מה", "עשה", "זה")} "and what did this one do?"; {SP_(286, 17, "כל", "היושב", "ואינו", "עובר", "עברה")} "whoever sits and does not transgress"; {SP_(286, 17, "נותנים", "לו", "שכר", "כעושה", "מצוה")} "they give him reward as one who does a commandment"): Makkot 3:16\'s close (the English\'s "cf.") — Ezekiel 18 the kin of 24:16 (find 1) cited for the righteous man; the interest of 23:20 in the psalm; the piska\'s last row. Fresh.')
srow(287, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"MUZZLE NOT AN OX" (25:4) — ONLY AN OX? OTHER CATTLE, BEASTS AND BIRDS AS THE OX WHENCE? "MUZZLE NOT" — ANY; WHY "OX"? AN OX YOU MAY NOT MUZZLE, A MAN YOU MAY. The head row of piska 287 ({SP_(287, 1, "שאר", "בהמה", "חיה", "ועוף")} "other cattle, beasts and birds"; {SP_(287, 1, "שור", "אי", "אתה", "חוסם", "חוסם", "אתה", "את", "האדם")} "an ox you may not muzzle; a man you may muzzle"): the class every working animal (Bava Kamma 5:7 the English\'s "cf."), the laborer of 23:25 excluded — he may waive by agreement (Bava Metzia 7:6); the design\'s DV25-02. Fresh.')
srow(287, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN ITS THRESHING" — ONLY THRESHING? OTHER LABORS WHENCE? "MUZZLE NOT" — ANY; WHY "THRESHING"? AS THRESHING IS OF WHAT GROWS FROM THE EARTH, DETACHED FROM THE GROUND, AT THE WORK\'S COMPLETION, AND THE WORKER EATS — SO EVERY SUCH LABOR. ({SP_(287, 2, "לרבות", "שאר", "עבודות")} "to include other labors"; {SP_(287, 2, "שגדולו", "מן", "הארץ", "ותלוש", "מן", "הקרקע")} "which grows from the earth and is detached from the ground"; {SP_(287, 2, "בשעת", "גמר", "מלאכה")} "at the time of the work\'s completion"): THE FOUR CONDITIONS of the eating labor — Bava Metzia 7:2\'s row for the laborer (23:25-26) and the ox alike: one rule for the man\'s mouth and the beast\'s. Fresh.')
srow(287, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE B. R. JUDAH: AS THRESHING IS DONE WITH HANDS, FEET AND BODY — EXCLUDING WORK WITH THE HANDS BUT NOT THE FEET, THE FEET BUT NOT THE BODY. ({SP_(287, 3, "בידיו", "וברגליו", "ובגופו")} "with his hands, his feet and his body"; {SP_(287, 3, "יצא", "העושה", "בידיו", "אבל", "לא", "ברגליו")} "excluding one who works with his hands but not with his feet"): a narrower prototype disputed (the Tosefta\'s row the English names); one of chapter 25\'s two rows citing no verse (the ink). Fresh.')
